    {
      "id": "claim_aea23955cfe0485181e4ef5e006ca256",
      "statement": "The documented local run flow is: fill credentials into redis/redis_template.env and rename it to redis/redis.env, start the infrastructure with docker-compose up -d from a compose file instantiated from docker-compose-template.yaml, start the application, use Swagger UI at localhost:8080, and inspect data at localhost:5540 (docker-compose down stops it; redis-cli access via docker exec -it redis redis-cli plus AUTH). The instantiated docker-compose.yml, redis.env, redis.conf, redis.acl, .env, data/*, and redisinsight/* are all gitignored, and because the template only exposes 6379 inside the compose network, a host-run application using the default profile cannot reach the containerized Redis without publishing the port.",
